{
  // The product program (`xspec`). Compiled by `npm run build` to dist/;
  // dist/cli/bin.js is the `xspec` executable declared in package.json.
  //
  // The defineConfig module (SPEC 7.6) is the package's root entry, one file
  // per route that package.json's `exports` names:
  //   import   the ES module dist/index.mjs, compiled from index.mts, typed
  //            by dist/index.d.mts (which the top-level `types` also names,
  //            for TypeScript's `node10` resolution, which reads no
  //            `exports`). An `.mjs` file is an ES module by its extension
  //            alone, as it must be: Node.js reads no `type` from the manifest
  //            of a package installed as node_modules/node_modules, an
  //            installation name 7.6 covers, and 22.0 predates module-syntax
  //            detection, so a `.js` entry would load as CommonJS there and
  //            fail;
  //   require  the CommonJS module dist/index.cjs, compiled from index.cts,
  //            typed by dist/index.d.cts, so that the module loads through
  //            `require` with no option on every Node.js release 7.6 covers,
  //            22.0 through 22.11 included, where `require` cannot load an ES
  //            module. Hence `.mts` and `.cts` sources are compiled too.
  //
  // This project must never include files from test/ — the harness is a
  // separate program (TEST-SPEC H-2; IMPLEMENTATION.md).
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": ".",
    "outDir": "../dist",
    "declaration": true
  },
  "include": ["./**/*.ts", "./**/*.mts", "./**/*.cts"]
}
